%% M2 key flow 3: an admin changes the price of a lane.
%% A price change closes the card in force and adds a new one.
%% Quotes already issued keep their fee, because each holds its own Redis snapshot.
%% Simplified for the design report: the closure and the insert are shown as one
%% operation, and only the overlap guard is drawn.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Admin (browser)
    participant UI as Admin rate-card<br/>screen
    participant GW as api-gateway
    participant PS as pricing-service
    participant PG as Postgres

    A->>UI: close the card in force,<br/>publish the new price
    UI->>GW: PUT .../rate-cards/{id}/closure<br/>POST .../rate-cards
    GW->>PS: forward (ADMIN role<br/>required)
    PS->>PS: check the new period does not<br/>overlap the cards already in force
    alt no overlap
        PS->>PG: UPDATE effective_to,<br/>then INSERT the new card
        PG-->>PS: ok
        PS-->>UI: 201: both periods
    else an overlapping card exists
        PS-->>UI: 409 problem+json<br/>RATE_CARD_OVERLAP
    end
    UI-->>A: the old and new periods<br/>shown side by side
    Note over PS,PG: the old card is closed, never deleted, and quotes already<br/>issued keep their fee: their Redis snapshots are untouched
